From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apklayer: berberis.mode.<package>, the translation mode of one app

BERBERIS_MODE / berberis.mode set the mode of every translated app. PGR (Unity, arm64 on an x86_64 PC) draws its 3D home scene as
block noise in the default two-gear mode and cleanly lite-translated; the property berberis.mode.<package> (the package from the code
cache path native_bridge_initialize gets, set before InitBerberis) gives one app its mode while the others keep two-gear. The
environment still wins, then the app property, then berberis.mode.

diff --git a/base/config_globals.cc b/base/config_globals.cc
index 16857af7..d2b69100 100644
--- a/base/config_globals.cc
+++ b/base/config_globals.cc
@@ -234,9 +234,20 @@ const char* GetTracingConfig() {
   return var.get();
 }
 
+// apklayer patch: the app's own mode, berberis.mode.<package> (the code cache path's package, set before InitBerberis), before
+// berberis.mode; BERBERIS_MODE in the environment still wins. One app whose code the heavy tier miscompiles (PGR's home scene: block
+// noise in two-gear mode) runs lite-translated while the others keep two-gear (`apklayer prop set berberis.mode.<package> <mode>`).
 const char* GetTranslationModeConfig() {
-  static ConfigStr var("BERBERIS_MODE", "berberis.mode");
-  return var.get();
+  static const char* value = [] {
+    if (const char* package = GetAppPackageName(); package != nullptr) {
+      std::string prop = std::string("berberis.mode.") + package;
+      ConfigStr app("BERBERIS_MODE", prop.c_str());
+      if (app.get() != nullptr) return app.get();
+    }
+    ConfigStr var("BERBERIS_MODE", "berberis.mode");
+    return var.get();
+  }();
+  return value;
 }
 
 const char* GetProfilingConfig() {
